get 750 split equally, no mint, no validation · measure: all of hardest level, targets solved, bounty value, ROI, knowledge found (bits), knowledge per unit of money, money to the main level, waste · 30 runs per row.</p>\n<p><strong>Caveats:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>A simulation with guessed parameters: it shows how the rules play out, not that they work.</li>\n</ul>\n<details><summary>Details</summary><p>The simple model on a generated idea graph (10 levels × 10 ideas, 2.5 parents each, sequences of 4 bits growing by 3 per level, composition 0.7); each run draws its own graph. Only α and β vary. Held fixed: 12 identical agents, a budget of 750 split equally every round (f = 0), no flat mint, a knowledge reward of 1 per new bit flowing back with α, no validation.</p>\n<p>Values are mean ± standard deviation over runs.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>society</th>\n<th>budget</th>\n<th>frontier</th>\n<th>targets solved</th>\n<th>value gained</th>\n<th>ROI (value per spend)</th>\n<th>knowledge (bits)</th>\n<th>knowledge published (bits)</th>\n<th>bits per money</th>\n<th>cost</th>\n<th>waste</th>\n<th>sharing</th>\n<th>reach L10</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>Traditional (α = 1, β = 0)</td>\n<td>750</td>\n<td>0.0 ± 0.0</td>\n<td>0.0 ± 0.0</td>\n<td>0 ± 0</td>\n<td>0.00 ± 0.00</td>\n<td>40 ± 6</td>\n<td>0 ± 0</td>\n<td>0.054 ± 0.008</td>\n<td>–</td>\n<td>0.22 ± 0.06</td>\n<td>0.00 ± 0.00</td>\n<td>0.00</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Traditional (α = 1, β = 0)</td>\n<td>1500</td>\n<td>0.0 ± 0.0</td>\n<td>0.0 ± 0.0</td>\n<td>0 ± 0</td>\n<td>0.00 ± 0.00</td>\n<td>58 ± 9</td>\n<td>0 ± 0</td>\n<td>0.039 ± 0.006</td>\n<td>–</td>\n<td>0.33 ± 0.07</td>\n<td>0.00 ± 0.00</td>\n<td>0.00</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Traditional (α = 1, β = 0)</td>\n<td>3000</td>\n<td>0.0 ± 0.0</td>\n<td>0.0 ± 0.0</td>\n<td>0 ± 0</td>\n<td>0.00 ± 0.00</td>\n<td>85 ± 11</td>\n<td>0 ± 0</td>\n<td>0.029 ± 0.004</td>\n<td>–</td>\n<td>0.47 ± 0.05</td>\n<td>0.00 ± 0.00</td>\n<td>0.00</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Tra